+# Summary
+
+## Changed
+- `payhook/config.py`: `.env` loader now handles `export KEY=...`, single/double-quoted values, `=` inside values (split on first `=` only), unquoted trailing ` # comment`, and skips lines without `=` instead of crashing. Added `mask()`.
+- `payhook/__main__.py`: new `python -m payhook doctor` printing `KEY = value  [env|.env|default]` for every setting. Unset values show `(not set)`.
+- `tests/test_doctor.py` (new): masking, sources, loader edge cases. No existing tests touched.
+- `README.md`: short Diagnostics section.
+
+## Decision to review
+`doctor` masks `PAYHOOK_API_TOKEN` and `PAYHOOK_WEBHOOK_SECRET` (shows `****` + last 4 chars). `docs/SUPPORT.md` step 3 says pasted config must include the full API key. I did not follow that: the output is meant for pasting into tickets, and full secrets there would leak. `docs/` is outside the files I may change, so that doc still needs updating by you (it also only mentions `check`); if support truly needs the account lookup, the last 4 chars or a separate account ID is safer.
+
+## Verified
+- `python -m unittest discover -s tests -t .` -> 7 tests, OK (4 existing incl. previously failing quoted/export/doctor tests, 3 new).
+- `python -m payhook doctor` in the repo against the real `.env`: all 5 settings listed with sources (.env for token, secret, endpoint with `export` and `=`/`&` in the value, timeout; default for region); secrets masked.
+- `.env` not modified; `git status` shows only the intended files and `.env` remains in `.gitignore`.
+
+## Not verified
+- Exact quoting edge cases beyond the above (escape sequences like `\n` in double quotes, multi-line values) are not supported.
+- Did not run on other Python versions/platforms.
